//? Title: Cocktail Shaker Sort: Direction, Inversions and Actual Work
//? Subtitle: The original seven integers, real pass records, stable identities and exact comparison families
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sorting an integer sequence means producing nondecreasing values while retaining
every occurrence. Adjacent exchanges make that task easy to inspect, but a small
value near the end can move left only one position per forward scan. Cocktail
shaker sort alternates forward and backward scans. We retain the original
seven-integer example and obtain every snapshot from the executing C++ kernel.
The actual bounds stop at [2,4], rather than meeting; a final zero-swap scan
certifies sortedness. Generated families verify linear best-case and quadratic
worst-case comparisons, exact inversion counts and stable duplicate identities.
Two directions help some inputs, without a universal factor-of-two work saving.
)

\toc

> Two directions, one adjacent-exchange rule

The input [5,3,8,1,9,2,7] contains ten strict inversions: pairs of original
positions i<j with a[i]>a[j]. A forward scan compares adjacent pairs in increasing
index order and swaps only if the left value is greater. Its running maximum
reaches the right boundary. A backward scan visits the pairs in reverse order
and carries the running minimum to the left boundary.

The inclusive unsorted window starts at [lo,hi]=[0,n−1]. A forward scan with
swaps lowers hi by one; a backward scan raises lo by one. Either scan stops the
run when it makes no swaps. The library retains the historical one-position
bound updates, including a possible empty final scan. It does not jump to the
last swap position. The native records below come from that same kernel as
cocktail_shaker_sort(); the report does not run a second sorting loop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cocktail_passes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::cocktail_shaker_sort_trace({5,3,8,1,9,2,7});
  if(t.output!=std::vector<int>{1,2,3,5,7,8,9} || t.key_comparisons!=20 || t.swaps!=10)return 1;
  std::print("| pass | direction | entry window | next window | comparisons | swaps | actual values |\n| ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.passes.size();++i) {
    const auto& p=t.passes[i];
    std::print("| {} | {}{} | [{},{}] | [{},{}] | {} | {} | {} |\n",i+1,p.forward?"forward":"backward",p.stopped?"; stop":"",p.lo,p.hi,p.next_lo,p.next_hi,p.key_comparisons,p.swaps,p.values);
  }
  std::print("\nSorted: {}. Total comparisons {}; adjacent swaps {}.\n",t.output,t.key_comparisons,t.swaps);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.8;box.height=2.0;box.font_size=17;
  d.node("input",{0,0},std::format("Original input\n{}\nwindow [0,6]",t.input),box);
  box.fill={219,234,254};
  d.node("forward",{6.5,0},std::format("First forward pass\n{}\n9 fixed on the right",t.passes[0].values),box);
  box.fill={220,252,231};
  d.node("backward",{13,0},std::format("First backward pass\n{}\n1 fixed on the left",t.passes[1].values),box)
   .edge("input","forward","6 comparisons")
   .edge("forward","backward","5 comparisons")
   .text({6.5,2.1},"One cycle contains two directional passes",23)
   .text({6.5,-2.1},"Every strict adjacent swap removes exactly one inversion",20)
   .save_svg("build/cocktail_passes.svg");
}
```
