\caption(Actual post-pass bounds include the unchanged terminal interval. The unsorted-window invariant permits early termination before the bounds meet.)
\alttext(The lower blue bound rises from zero to two and the upper red bound falls from six to four. Both remain constant on the fifth, zero-swap pass.)

> Exact best, worst and misplaced-end families

For n≥2, the first pass performs n−1 key comparisons. If the input is already
sorted, including an all-equal input, none swap and that is the complete cost.
Each subsequent pass has one fewer comparison. Hence the worst possible count
is the triangular sum below. Reverse distinct input attains it and also has
that many inversions. The historical kernel records a final zero-comparison
pass in this case; that record changes pass counts, but not key work.

\[
n-1\le C(a)\le(n-1)+(n-2)+\cdots+1=\frac{n(n-1)}2.
\]
\alttext(For at least two items, key comparisons lie between n-minus-one and the triangular sum n times n-minus-one divided by two. Sorted input attains the lower bound and reversed distinct input the upper bound.)

Now fix n≥3. A turtle input [1,2,...,n−1,0] has just n−1 inversions. The first
forward pass moves zero left one position, the backward pass carries it all
the way to the start, and a final forward scan certifies the remaining window.
The lengths n−1, n−2 and n−3 give C=3n−6. A forward-only bubble sort that
shrinks its right end by one and stops after a zero-swap pass needs n−1 swapping
passes on this turtle, with n(n−1)/2 comparisons. This follows because zero can
move left only once per forward pass. Here reversing direction changes
quadratic work into linear work, rather than merely halving it.

For the rabbit [n−1,0,1,...,n−2], the first forward pass already sorts the input;
the following backward scan stops, giving C=2n−3. A forward-only variant's
second forward scan has the same length, so it has the same comparison count.
Reverse order is quadratic for both methods. There is no uniform work ratio.
Even one inversion can require a second linear scan; inversion count determines
swaps, while the placement of inversions also influences comparisons.

The next experiment constructs these exact integer families with standard
sequence operations. No external dataset is useful for isolating these bounds.
The tables and plots use actual native counters, with assertions against all
four closed forms; values are key comparisons, excluding loop tests, copies
and trace allocation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cocktail_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> sizes,best,worst,turtle_work,rabbit_work;
  std::print("| n | sorted comparisons | reverse comparisons | turtle comparisons | rabbit comparisons | turtle swaps |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const std::size_t n:{8,16,32,64,128}) {
    std::vector<int> a(n);std::iota(a.begin(),a.end(),0);
    const auto sorted=dm::algorithms::cocktail_shaker_sort_trace(a);
    std::reverse(a.begin(),a.end());const auto reversed=dm::algorithms::cocktail_shaker_sort_trace(a);
    std::iota(a.begin(),a.end()-1,1);a.back()=0;
    const auto turtle=dm::algorithms::cocktail_shaker_sort_trace(a);
    a[0]=static_cast<int>(n-1);std::iota(a.begin()+1,a.end(),0);
    const auto rabbit=dm::algorithms::cocktail_shaker_sort_trace(a);
    if(sorted.key_comparisons!=n-1 || reversed.key_comparisons!=n*(n-1)/2 || turtle.key_comparisons!=3*n-6 || rabbit.key_comparisons!=2*n-3 || turtle.swaps!=n-1)return 1;
    sizes.push_back(n);best.push_back(sorted.key_comparisons);worst.push_back(reversed.key_comparisons);
    turtle_work.push_back(turtle.key_comparisons);rabbit_work.push_back(rabbit.key_comparisons);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,sorted.key_comparisons,reversed.key_comparisons,turtle.key_comparisons,rabbit.key_comparisons,turtle.swaps);
  }
  auto quadratic=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),linear=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  quadratic.line(sizes,worst,"reverse",{220,38,38},2).points(sizes,worst,"reverse",{220,38,38},5)
      .legend({"reverse"},{{220,38,38}}).y_limits(0,10000)
      .title("Reverse: n(n-1)/2 comparisons").x_label("input length n").y_label("key comparisons");
  linear.line(sizes,best,"sorted",{22,163,74},2).line(sizes,turtle_work,"turtle",{37,99,235},2)
      .line(sizes,rabbit_work,"rabbit",{234,88,12},2)
      .legend({"sorted","turtle","rabbit"},{{22,163,74},{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
      .title("Three linear families").x_label("input length n").y_label("key comparisons").y_limits(0,450);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2);
  layout.add(quadratic).add(linear).size(1100,470).fit_panels().save_svg("build/cocktail_work.svg");
}
```
