> Stability is about identities, not only equal integers

An integer-only sorted vector cannot distinguish repeated occurrences. The
trace therefore carries original zero-based positions through the very same
swaps. For [2,1,2,1,2], the two ones must emerge with original positions [1,3]
and the three twos with [0,2,4]. Equal values can change position when a smaller
or larger value crosses them, but two equal occurrences can reverse their order
only by crossing each other. The strict comparison never exchanges such a pair,
so their order is stable throughout the run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cocktail_stability.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::cocktail_shaker_sort_trace({2,1,2,1,2});
  if(t.original_indices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{1,3,0,2,4})return 1;
  std::print("| sorted position | value | original position |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(70,1000);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=1.6;box.height=1;box.font_size=18;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.input.size();++i) {
    box.fill=t.input[i]==1?dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
    d.node(std::format("in{}",i),{2.3*i,1.5},std::format("{}\nsource {}",t.input[i],i),box);
    box.fill=t.output[i]==1?dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
    d.node(std::format("out{}",i),{2.3*i,-1.5},std::format("{}\nsource {}",t.output[i],t.original_indices[i]),box);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",i,t.output[i],t.original_indices[i]);
  }
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.output.size();++i)
    d.edge(std::format("in{}",t.original_indices[i]),std::format("out{}",i));
  d.text({4.6,3},"Actual source identities survive the adjacent exchanges",22)
   .text({4.6,-3},"Ones retain [1,3]; twos retain [0,2,4]",21)
   .save_svg("build/cocktail_stability.svg");
  std::print("\nStrict inversion count and measured swaps: {}.\n",t.swaps);
}
```
